From: Droidloom development build
Subject: [PATCH] health: battery polls never wake the host

The health loop polls the battery from a CLOCK_BOOTTIME_ALARM timer, every
60 s on a charger and every 600 s on battery. In a Droidloom cell that alarm
is armed on the host's RTC, so an idle cell woke the phone out of s2idle at
each poll.

The loop now polls from CLOCK_BOOTTIME. While the host is awake nothing
changes; a poll that falls due in suspend runs at resume. Power-supply
uevents still update the battery at once. Without the alarm the service no
longer needs CAP_WAKE_ALARM.

diff --git a/health/aidl/default/android.hardware.health-service.example.rc b/health/aidl/default/android.hardware.health-service.example.rc
index e052024..0e99c47 100644
--- a/health/aidl/default/android.hardware.health-service.example.rc
+++ b/health/aidl/default/android.hardware.health-service.example.rc
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@ service vendor.health-default /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.health-service.exa
     class hal
     user system
     group system
-    capabilities WAKE_ALARM BLOCK_SUSPEND
+    capabilities BLOCK_SUSPEND
     file /dev/kmsg w
 
 service vendor.charger /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.health-service.example --charger
diff --git a/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp b/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp
index 8501f33..c99a545 100644
--- a/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp
+++ b/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp
@@ -231,7 +231,9 @@ void HealthLoop::WakeAlarmEvent(uint32_t /*epevents*/) {
 }
 
 void HealthLoop::WakeAlarmInit(void) {
-    wakealarm_fd_.reset(timerfd_create(CLOCK_BOOTTIME_ALARM, TFD_NONBLOCK));
+    // Droidloom: the cell shares the host's suspend. A battery poll must never
+    // wake the host; a poll that falls due in suspend runs at resume.
+    wakealarm_fd_.reset(timerfd_create(CLOCK_BOOTTIME, TFD_NONBLOCK));
     if (wakealarm_fd_ == -1) {
         KLOG_ERROR(LOG_TAG, "wakealarm_init: timerfd_create failed\n");
         return;
